#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096843 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096402 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a312840-0d35-50bb-94b3-b04778f4efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Function Using the Chain Rule and Prime Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "2c37ae73-233d-5e0d-87ff-05cacc6d078b" :question/math-academy-id "e-183" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{1-3x}},$ calculate $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=1-3x$ and $f(g(x)) = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{g}} = g^{-1/2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{-1/2}{)}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2}{g}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2{g}^{3/2}}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(1-3x{)}^{′}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{g}^{3/2}}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2{g}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2(1-3x{)}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a312840-0d35-50bb-94b3-b04778f4efc3" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493336 :question-generator/id #uuid "f62990ef-82f5-5028-b79d-43e7f23bfce3" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186096843.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a312840-0d35-50bb-94b3-b04778f4efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Function Using the Chain Rule and Prime Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd726c27-0178-5cc8-a8b6-82e60d62ac1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(15x^{4} - 8x)(3x^{5} - 4x^{2})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093807} {:answer/id #uuid "c477f2d6-5ad8-52b3-8fe5-92a70939ea8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(5x^{5} - 8x)(3x^{5} - 4x^{2})^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186093808} {:answer/id #uuid "060329dc-443f-5ee6-a297-ff049fb57b80" :answer/type {:db/ide