58e18e" :question/math-academy-id "q-107293" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(3x+4)}^{5},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=3x+4$ and $f(g(x))=g(x{)}^{5}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{5}{)}^{′}=5{g}^{4}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(3x+4{)}^{′}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =5{g}^{4}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =15(3x+4{)}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a312840-0d35-50bb-94b3-b04778f4efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Function Using the Chain Rule and Prime Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc8b5aee-000a-5a8d-818f-e20c5debd3ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20(4x+3)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc8b5aee-000a-5a8d-818f-e20c5debd3ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20(4x+3)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316184} :answer-field/id #uuid "625a79d7-54d7-570b-aa7c-729d582ac660" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ebc59fe-5ccc-59b1-9757-9c760459c2ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-342804" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(4x+3)}^{5},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=4x+3$ and $f(g(x))=g(x{)}^{5}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{5}{)}^{′}=5{g}^{4}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(4x+3{)}^{′}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =5{g}^{4}\\cdot (4) \\\\  & =20(4x+3{)}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317333 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a312840-0d35-50bb-94b3-b04778f4efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Function Using the Chain Rule and Prime Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8817f05b-018c-5853-b6cc-e00880617a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8817f05b-018c-5853-b6cc-e00880617a94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315880} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5ab2d60-fecd-56b2-a6fc-370a03381af0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317093}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2fb4db78-694f-5845-af11-624db7bcff81" :question/math-academy-id "q-342875" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={({x}^{5}-4{x}^{4})}^{2},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=2({x}^{5}-4{x}^{4})($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)={x}^{5}-4{x}^{4}$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{2})^{′}=2g, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{5}-4{x}^{4})^{′}=5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =2g\\cdot (5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{5}-4{x}^{4})(\\,5{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317335 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a312840-0d35-50bb-94b3-b04778f4efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Function Using the Chain Rule and Prime Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54037730-2600-58cb-b40d-648fd184a076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54037730-2600-58cb-b40d-648fd184a076" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315600} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f9abe6a-bb3b-59b2-9f07-73fdde4dcc36" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6a140a75-4d09-557b-baa7-d7202838dd2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-342883" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\sqrt{5x-4},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=5x-4$ and $f(g(x))=\\sqrt{g(x)}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & ={(\\sqrt{g})}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(5x-4)^{′}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317336 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a312840-0d35-50bb-94b3-b04778f4efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Function Using the Chain Rule and Prime Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d665e027-6ab2-5ec3-82b7-84f4dddc219b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-4{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d665e027-6ab2-5ec3-82b7-84f4dddc219b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-4{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316315} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1297ade-d13c-5373-bff2-2ee35469ee63" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317084}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "49fe03e2-8c48-5c16-b76a-8505b327ec2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-342891" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5}},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5{)}^{3}}}($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5$ and $f(g(x))=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{g(x)}}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & ={(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{g}})}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{g}^{3}}}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5{)}^{′}=8{x}^{3}-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{g}^{3}}}\\cdot (8{x}^{3}-2x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2{x}^{4}-{x}^{2}+5{)}^{3}}}(\\,x-4{x}^{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339021 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a312840-0d35-50bb-94b3-b04778f4efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Function Using the Chain Rule and Prime Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c5aa34c-8035-515e-9a22-0910ed15b1fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32(16x-7{)}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336452} {:answer/id #uuid "8dec9f04-7eaf-5206-a8d3-7559c929a68c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16(8x-7{)}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337312} {:answer/id #uuid "be24eea7-2334-5d10-9f49-6df8807cf6b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16(16x-7{)}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337721} {:answer/id #uuid "d7e1b6c9-7b2d-5b89-b492-99eacd8fa4bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8(8x-7{)}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337907} {:answer/id #uuid "fb4036bb-195b-5a9c-b701-d3dee3bfbc0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32(8x-7{)}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb4036bb-195b-5a9c-b701-d3dee3bfbc0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32(8x-7{)}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338239} :answer-field/id #uuid "37b56870-5595-52b0-ae23-7f96f4a87f21" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "217bdf0c-2bc6-585f-ac52-fad4aec9092f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71954" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(8x-7)}^{4},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=8x-7$ and $f(g(x))=g(x{)}^{4}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{4}{)}^{′}=4{g}^{3}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(8x-7{)}^{′}=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =4{g}^{3}\\cdot (8) \\\\  & =32(8x-7{)}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a312840-0d35-50bb-94b3-b04778f4efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Function Using the Chain Rule and Prime Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d2f6517-e258-513a-b912-2250e7c54e17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15(2+5x{)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336461} {:answer/id #uuid "3b2c8729-231c-5b49-a873-246a32aa4645" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15(2-5x{)}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336588} {:answer/id #uuid "77d335ef-89db-5392-8e96-2e5663d37f72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15(2+5x{)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337111} {:answer/id #uuid "84c34e15-f7f7-51bd-91ad-be1849bcac42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15(2-5x{)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337229} {:answer/id #uuid "ba6755f1-59bc-5601-b289-66317d2b0d63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15(2-5x{)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba6755f1-59bc-5601-b289-66317d2b0d63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15(2-5x{)}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337682} :answer-field/id #uuid "20dca297-5492-547a-957c-959f9e7520f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338339}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ccad926b-6344-5bec-99bc-507d50cda1e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-71956" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(2-5x)}^{3},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=2-5x$ and $f(g(x))=g(x{)}^{3}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{3}{)}^{′}=3{g}^{2}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(2-5x{)}^{′}=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =3{g}^{2}\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-15(2-5x{)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a312840-0d35-50bb-94b3-b04778f4efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Function Using the Chain Rule and Prime Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1f60e01-bcaa-538a-85d1-4c41aee48064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20(4x+6)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1f60e01-bcaa-538a-85d1-4c41aee48064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20(4x+6)^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493335} :answer-field/id #uuid "74945d2f-3779-5856-8f0b-b1fe26940f82" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493329}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c698fb8-2f47-52aa-ab20-d02b17699d11" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={(4x+6)}^{5},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=4x+6$ and $f(g(x))=g(x{)}^{5}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{5}{)}^{′}=5{g}^{4}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(4x+6{)}^{′}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =5{g}^{4}\\cdot (4) \\\\  & =20(4x+6{)}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493331 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a312840-0d35-50bb-94b3-b04778f4efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Function Using the Chain Rule and Prime Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e6b327a-95b5-56cb-b8b1-80852501eb0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e6b327a-95b5-56cb-b8b1-80852501eb0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493327} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a534b2c-8471-58d8-901e-8ca326167938" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "97e8ab80-425a-5ce3-aeca-1b6c32080f6d" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\sqrt{5x-3},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=5x-3$ and $f(g(x))=\\sqrt{g(x)}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & ={(\\sqrt{g})}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =(5x-3)^{′}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{g}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5x-3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0a312840-0d35-50bb-94b3-b04778f4efc3" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Function Using the Chain Rule and Prime Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df5e2ea6-5eec-545e-bf02-640b9eb005aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df5e2ea6-5eec-545e-bf02-640b9eb005aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493334} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9beb5af-bf72-501b-8c38-28d625a4d182" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a645231c-c79c-561b-9b41-b96c53332e19" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})}^{2},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=2({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})($\n{{field-1}}\n$)$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)={x}^{5}-7{x}^{4}$ and $f(g(x))=g(x)^{2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(g(x)) & =({g}^{2})^{′}=2g, \\\\ {g}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})^{′}=5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={f}^{′}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =2g\\cdot (5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2({x}^{5}-7{x}^{4})(\\,5{x}^{4}-28{x}^{3}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Function Using the Chain Rule and Prime Notation"}]}
